 "#": "A game that makes its device again mid-run (run.py --cases gfx-d3d11-new-device,gfx-d3d11-eyes-two-devices,gfx-d3d12-new-device,gfx-vk-new-device --script scripts/gfx_all_apis.json --expect expect/gfx_new_device.json): 512 x 512 frames of its first device, then 576 x 576 ones of a new device. D3D11: the session is made again on the new device and shows them. D3D12's second device is on WARP (D3D12 has one device per adapter), which isn't the runtime's adapter: the runtime refuses its session, and the frames are left out (104, TextureIsOnWrongDevice); with WARP the only adapter, as on CI, that case is skipped. Vulkan isn't followed: the new device's frames are refused (102, InvalidTexture). The game is never told to quit. gfx-d3d11-eyes-two-devices: the left eye on one device and the right on another: the session follows a few times, ending on the right eye's device, and the left is then left out (104); no frame names a swapchain of a session that's gone.",
